NAME='Jupiter'
COVER_SUB='How you grow and where luck finds you, sign by sign.'
T=[
('Bold · 2022–23 · 2034–35','Jupiter in Aries, when harmonious or neutral, brings enthusiasm and independence, a loyal, sincere, altruistic spirit, will and organising ability, ambition and a sense of opportunity. Judgement is strongly marked, often severe, yet ready for clemency when there is good reason. Jyotish counts Mars as a friend of Jupiter. Karmic reading: a soul whose faith grows by acting and leading. The shadow is overconfidence and impatience. The lesson: faith works best with a plan.'),
('Abundant · 2023–24 · 2035–36','Jupiter in Taurus, when harmonious, gives a practical mind and good sense, an indulgence that can verge on weakness, a love of comfort, good food and the pleasures of life. It favours earnings and brings an uncommon economic skill and financial prosperity, with trade in food, wine and farming. Jyotish counts Venus as an enemy of Jupiter. Karmic reading: a soul learning that abundance is held, not hoarded. The shadow is indulgence and complacency. The lesson: enough is a real amount.'),
('Detriment · 2024–25 · 2036–37','Jupiter in Gemini is in detriment: with harmony it still gives open-mindedness and literary, scientific and commercial talent. You are courteous, sociable and eloquent, sought by your entourage, with success in journalism, teaching and trade. Jyotish counts Mercury as an enemy of Jupiter, so wisdom and cleverness can argue. Curiosity is large, focus small. Karmic reading: a soul learning to turn information into wisdom. The shadow is scattered beliefs. The lesson: choose the idea worth following to the end.'),
('Exalted · 2025–26 · 2037–38','Jupiter is exalted in Cancer, and Jyotish agrees, placing its peak at 5°. It gives a cheerful character and an accommodating spirit that develops imagination and intuition, a keen sense of family and of traditional values. You do not like to suffer or to see suffering, and you are charitable and relieve the pain of others. Karmic reading: a soul that has earned its protective gifts. The shadow is overprotection and sentimentality. The lesson: nourishing others is easiest when you are fed yourself.'),
('Generous · 2026–27 · 2038–39','Jupiter in Leo is a sign of great vitality, ambition and intelligence free of prejudice or pettiness. It loves luxury, splendour and beauty, with nobility of spirit, optimism and a concern for reputation. Personal magnetism attracts the sympathy and favours of important people, with marriage or union to a rich or prominent partner. Jyotish counts the Sun as a friend of Jupiter. Karmic reading: a soul learning to lead with warmth. The shadow is pride and showing off. The lesson: the best leaders make others bigger.'),
('Detriment · 2015–16 · 2027–28','Jupiter in Virgo is in detriment: a patient nature suited to precision and finishing work, with a sense of organisation, a love of methodical study and detail, prudence in every move, objective judgement and great mental subtlety. Jyotish counts Mercury as an enemy of Jupiter. Wisdom comes through detail, service and craft, but the larger vision can be lost in the checklist. Karmic reading: a soul learning to trust the whole. The shadow is perfectionism and worry. The lesson: the whole is more than its parts.'),
('Sociable · 2016–17 · 2028–29','Jupiter in Libra, when harmonious or neutral, gives good humour, a loyal character and a love of peace and quiet. It influences favourably men of the law (lawyers, law professors, magistrates), and balance and fairness make excellent mediators and arbiters. Marriage brings notable satisfaction. Jyotish counts Venus as an enemy of Jupiter. Karmic reading: a soul learning justice through relationship. The shadow is indecision and overreliance on others. The lesson: wisdom is knowing what you want as well as what is fair.'),
('Deep · 2017–18 · 2029–30','Jupiter in Scorpio, when harmonious, gives good psychophysical balance, a particular attraction to esoteric science, an aptitude for medicine, and a bent for free professions where personal commitment, perseverance and self-trust bring success, with a talent for rebuilding after a setback. Jyotish counts Mars as a friend of Jupiter. Karmic reading: a soul that grows through crisis and rebirth. The shadow is obsession and secrecy. The lesson: abundance includes what you let go of.'),
('Own sign · 2018–19 · 2030–31','Jupiter is at home in Sagittarius, and Jyotish gives it own-sign and moolatrikona strength. In harmony it is a sign of wisdom: authoritative but with a paternal side, deep respect for family and tradition, an innate sympathy that brings friends and advantage, a love of sport, hunting, the open air and wide spaces. It is a free spirit. Volguine’s order of Jupiter is here a sense of meaning. Karmic reading: a soul that has earned its faith. The shadow is dogmatism. The lesson: a belief becomes wise when it can be questioned.'),
('Fall · 2019–20 · 2031–32','Jupiter is in its fall in Capricorn, and Jyotish marks its debilitation here at 5°. When harmonious it still gives thoughtfulness, a prudent and patient character and a balanced sense of measure and order. You are far-sighted, with a gift for organising and commanding, but little patience with subordinates, and you move with your own interests in view. Jyotish rates Saturn neutral toward Jupiter. Karmic reading: faith has to be earned through responsibility. The shadow is pessimism. The lesson: faith in the long road is also a kind of luck.'),
('Visionary · 2020–21 · 2032–33','Jupiter in Aquarius, when harmonious or neutral, gives good intellectual abilities and a bent for every discipline that opens new mental and spiritual horizons, including avant-garde science. A deep mind with concentration, coordination and synthesis. A lover of peace, you avoid arguments but do not like to be contradicted. Jyotish rates Saturn neutral. Karmic reading: a soul that believes in a better world and must serve it. The shadow is abstract idealism. The lesson: a better world also begins with someone close.'),
('Own sign · 2021–22 · 2033–34','Jupiter is at home in Pisces, and Jyotish gives it own-sign strength. In harmony it gives an amiable, sensitive character, attentive to helping and easing others’ pain: the protector of the weak. Basically traditional, it does all it can to keep domestic balance, with strong attachment to life and sorrow at the suffering of others. Karmic reading: a soul at the end of a long cycle, giving back what it has received. The shadow is naivety and escapism. The lesson: faith needs good boundaries.'),
]
